      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T17:41:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For representing the LATEST build_release (in mainline_module_sdks.py terms). Otherwise, when we build snapshots for the \"LATEST\" we filter out libraries which set min_sdk_version: \"current\" (either directly or if min_sdk_version is not set then it uses sdk_version: \"current\"). That is a problem because the sdk snapshot code treats \"LATEST\" as being \"Tiramisu\" and \"Tiramisu\" \u003c \"current\". So, a library with min_sdk_version: \"current\" is treated as not being supported on LATEST (Tiramisu) and so is excluded.\n\nI know that setting min_sdk_version: \"current\" is not something that is done for updatable mainline modules but it is used for other libraries, e.g. \"framework-bluetooth\" (which was updatable but was downgraded to non-updatable cs/android/packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/Android.bp?l\u003d7). It is also used by libraries used in other (non-mainline) sdk platform modules like i18n.",
      "parentUuid": "ccb1ba6d_dcaf78ee",
      "revId": "33accf8680497ee7e596ca11d5b0d943fe26dfc9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
